Z||000000||fieroshop||04-26-2000||04:20 PM||||Finally I will have a drill guide for 3.4 conversions. After more then six months of looking and trying to find somebody to make me a drill guide for 3.4 conversions I will have one today. I will also be able to sell these to people that want one and maybe even renting them out for the do it yourselfer's. I will know shortly how much they will cost, but from what the machine shop told me they will not cost an arm and a leg. More likely a tooth. Seriously it seems very reasonable. If any of you are interested in one or even to rent one let me know? ||||reg||7
Z||000001||mrfixit58||04-26-2000||04:35 PM||||A rental unit sounds interesting. I can't see me needing it more than once. I already have a 3.4 block and was thinking of just drilling it myself using the starter as a guide.<P>Please keep us posted,<BR>Roy||||reg||1
Z||000002||fieroshop||04-26-2000||05:05 PM||||Roy in answer to your question as to using the starter motor to drill, there is a problem with that. If you do not position the starter just right you may be off a few thousands of an inch and that could mean problems with being able to start your engine. My machine shop told me that to do it that way he would not guarantee that the starter would engage properly.||||reg||1
